\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces End-to-end architecture and tensor flow of MobilePIXORNeXt. Unordered 3D LiDAR point clouds pass through the parameter-free Strata-BEV14 rasterizer into a 14-channel statistical BEV tensor $\mathbf  {X} \in \mathbb  {R}^{B \times 14 \times 800 \times 704}$ without learned pillar encoders. ConvNeXt-style stages with parameter-free Block-SimAM attention extract multi-scale features. A top-down Scale-Gated Feature Pyramid Network (SG-FPN) fuses them into a 32-channel shared representation at stride 4 ($200 \times 176$). Decoupled GroupedHeader towers process Car and Pedestrian/Cyclist categories independently. Solid arrows show the feedforward inference path. Dashed arrows show training-only Oriented Geometric Alignment (OGA), IoU-Aware Quality Alignment (IQA), and Temperature-Softmax Bounded Uncertainty Weighting (T-SBUW).}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:r37_overview}{{1}{3}{End-to-end architecture and tensor flow of MobilePIXORNeXt. Unordered 3D LiDAR point clouds pass through the parameter-free Strata-BEV14 rasterizer into a 14-channel statistical BEV tensor $\mathbf {X} \in \mathbb {R}^{B \times 14 \times 800 \times 704}$ without learned pillar encoders. ConvNeXt-style stages with parameter-free Block-SimAM attention extract multi-scale features. A top-down Scale-Gated Feature Pyramid Network (SG-FPN) fuses them into a 32-channel shared representation at stride 4 ($200 \times 176$). Decoupled GroupedHeader towers process Car and Pedestrian/Cyclist categories independently. Solid arrows show the feedforward inference path. Dashed arrows show training-only Oriented Geometric Alignment (OGA), IoU-Aware Quality Alignment (IQA), and Temperature-Softmax Bounded Uncertainty Weighting (T-SBUW)}{figure.1}{}}
