\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Fourteen deterministic feature channels in the Strata-BEV14 representation for a KITTI driving scene ($800 \times 704$ grid at $0.1\,\text  {m}$ resolution). Channels 0--3 encode logarithmic point densities across four vertical strata ($[-2.5, 1.0]\,\text  {m}$). Channels 4--7 encode normalized maximum elevation $z_{\max }$, mean elevation $z_{\mathrm  {mean}}$, elevation span $z_{\mathrm  {span}}$, and population standard deviation $z_{\mathrm  {std}}$. Channels 8--9 encode maximum and mean reflectance intensity. Channel 10 records total cell logarithmic density, and Channel 11 records binary occupancy. Channels 12--13 preserve continuous horizontal subcell centroid displacements $(\Delta \bar  {x}, \Delta \bar  {y}) \in [-0.5, 0.5]$ to reduce discretization error. Brighter values indicate higher point concentrations, reflectance, or vertical dispersion.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:strata_bev14}{{2}{6}{Fourteen deterministic feature channels in the Strata-BEV14 representation for a KITTI driving scene ($800 \times 704$ grid at $0.1\,\text {m}$ resolution). Channels 0--3 encode logarithmic point densities across four vertical strata ($[-2.5, 1.0]\,\text {m}$). Channels 4--7 encode normalized maximum elevation $z_{\max }$, mean elevation $z_{\mathrm {mean}}$, elevation span $z_{\mathrm {span}}$, and population standard deviation $z_{\mathrm {std}}$. Channels 8--9 encode maximum and mean reflectance intensity. Channel 10 records total cell logarithmic density, and Channel 11 records binary occupancy. Channels 12--13 preserve continuous horizontal subcell centroid displacements $(\Delta \bar {x}, \Delta \bar {y}) \in [-0.5, 0.5]$ to reduce discretization error. Brighter values indicate higher point concentrations, reflectance, or vertical dispersion}{figure.2}{}}
